  "summary": "MRCL2 exfiltrates working-directory listing to a remote tunnel on import",
  "details": "MRCL2/__init__.py loads core.py, which at module load time enumerates the current working directory via os.listdir('.') and transmits the file list over a TCP socket to the hardcoded host zpxpq-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link on port 41379 — a free pinggy.link reverse-tunnel endpoint unrelated to the package's stated 'document integrity utility' purpose. The exfiltration fires on any `import MRCL2`, including in REPLs, CI jobs, and production processes, without any caller action beyond importing the package.",
